.TH JS 1
.SH NAME
js \- run JavaScript
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B js
[
.B -p
] [
.B -m
] [
.B -t
] [
.B -P
] [
.B -g
.I n
] [
.B -e
.I source
] [
.I file ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Js
runs JavaScript (ECMAScript 2025) in a realm of InferNode's engine.
Each
.I file
(a module, with
.BR -m ),
then each
.B -e
.IR source ,
runs in turn in the one realm, and then the promise jobs it queued.
With neither,
.I js
reads statements from its standard input and prints each one's value;
a statement not yet complete continues on the next line.
.PP
The realm has the language's built-ins and
.BR print ,
which writes its arguments and a newline to the standard output.
A module imports others by path, relative to its own.
.PP
The options are:
.TF -g\ n
.TP
.B -p
Print each file's or source's completion value.
.TP
.B -m
Run the files as modules.
.TP
.B -t
Say on the standard error how long each took.
.TP
.B -P
Sample where the realm is every 5 ms, and print where the time went, by
function, at the end.
.TP
.BI -g " n
Collect garbage after every
.I n
allocations, to find values the collector cannot see (engine testing).
.PD
.PP
An uncaught exception is printed on the standard error, and
.I js
exits with an error status.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
; js -p -e '[1, 2, 3].map(x => x ** 2)'
1,4,9
; js -m main.js
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/js.b
.br
.B /appl/lib/js
